From 9dd2dab37e91ab4b000802d98aa7c4713836d53a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Boccassi <luca.boccassi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 18:22:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rm-rf: fail closed when the root check fails

path_is_root_at() returns a negative errno when it cannot determine whether
a target is the root file system. rm_rf_at() treats those errors as a
negative answer and continued with destructive operations.

Propagate root-check errors before modifying the target, while preserving
REMOVE_MISSING_OK for an absent path.

Follow-up for c0228b4fa3e4e633afa5eb8417e6cd3e311cd250

Description: rm-rf: fail closed when the root check fails
 Backport upstream commit 9dd2dab37e91ab4b000802d98aa7c4713836d53a to v255.
 path_is_root_at() returns a negative errno when it cannot determine whether
 a target is the root file system; rm_rf_at() treated those errors as a
 negative answer and continued with destructive operations, which could
 remove the root file system when the root check failed.
 .
 Adapt the upstream test to the v255 API: src/shared/tests.h does not provide
 the ASSERT_OK/ASSERT_OK_ERRNO/ASSERT_ERROR_ERRNO macros, so translate the
 new rm_rf_dangling_symlink test assertions to assert_se().
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/systemd/systemd/commit/9dd2dab37e91ab4b000802d98aa7c4713836d53a
Bug: https://github.com/systemd/systemd/pull/42978
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-16

diff --git a/src/shared/rm-rf.c b/src/shared/rm-rf.c
index 573d6aeb04..56a56ed9ab 100644
--- a/src/shared/rm-rf.c
+++ b/src/shared/rm-rf.c
@@ -443,7 +443,20 @@ int rm_rf_at(int dir_fd, const char *path, RemoveFlags flags) {
 
         /* We refuse to clean the root file system with this call. This is extra paranoia to never cause a
          * really seriously broken system. */
-        if (path_is_root_at(dir_fd, path) > 0)
+        r = path_is_root_at(dir_fd, path);
+        if (r == -ENOENT) {
+                struct stat st;
+
+                if (fstatat(dir_fd, path, &st, AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW) < 0)
+                        r = -errno;
+                else
+                        r = 0; /* The entry exists, but is most likely a dangling symlink. */
+        }
+        if (FLAGS_SET(flags, REMOVE_MISSING_OK) && r == -ENOENT)
+                return 0;
+        if (r < 0)
+                return log_error_errno(r, "Failed to determine whether '%s' is the root file system: %m", path);
+        if (r > 0)
                 return log_error_errno(SYNTHETIC_ERRNO(EPERM),
                                        "Attempted to remove entire root file system, and we can't allow that.");
 
diff --git a/src/test/test-rm-rf.c b/src/test/test-rm-rf.c
index d029f608e2..15d1f32185 100644
--- a/src/test/test-rm-rf.c
+++ b/src/test/test-rm-rf.c
@@ -119,4 +119,20 @@ TEST(rm_rf_chmod) {
         test_rm_rf_chmod_inner();
 }
 
+TEST(rm_rf_dangling_symlink) {
+        _cleanup_(rm_rf_physical_and_freep) char *d = NULL;
+        const char *link;
+
+        assert_se(mkdtemp_malloc("/tmp/test-rm-rf-dangling.XXXXXXX", &d) >= 0);
+        link = strjoina(d, "/link");
+
+        assert_se(symlink("missing", link) >= 0);
+        assert_se(rm_rf(link, REMOVE_ROOT|REMOVE_PHYSICAL) >= 0);
+        assert_se(lstat(link, &(struct stat) {}) < 0 && errno == ENOENT);
+
+        assert_se(symlink("missing", link) >= 0);
+        assert_se(rm_rf(link, REMOVE_ROOT|REMOVE_PHYSICAL|REMOVE_MISSING_OK) >= 0);
+        assert_se(lstat(link, &(struct stat) {}) < 0 && errno == ENOENT);
+}
+
 DEFINE_TEST_MAIN(LOG_DEBUG);

